{"author":"Unknown","author_email":"","data":{"content_hash":"df75ff65def196cdadc591d2ccd01e3b77927200e5bd78b03d323bacce0fe3ea","digest":{"component_or_area":"release pipeline and store compatibility","key_entities":["release.yml","store-format-version","COMMIT","wheel","sdist","gerrit-verify.yaml","pyproject.toml","server.json","TICKETS_TRACKER_DIR","REBAR_MCP_ALLOW_RECONCILE_LIVE","verify.require_verdict_for_close","mcp-publisher","docs/releasing.md","docs/migrations.md"],"problem_keywords":["release integrity","store compatibility","security boundary","code review gate","v1.0 readiness","artifact provenance","build consistency","configuration validation","mutable references","removed inputs"],"propositions":["Release publication via v* tags lacks proof that the tagged SHA is reviewed-and-landed main, creating a control gap outside the Gerrit two-vote gate","No committed store-format-version record exists, preventing v1.0 and later binaries from failing closed on incompatible stores; absent-record must be treated as legacy format (fail-open) to preserve upgrade-in-place","Build artifacts bake COMMIT=None into wheels via sdist-from-source path and CI installs source tree instead of artifacts, hiding the defect until post-PyPI publication","Release pipeline resolves actions, build tools, and OIDC-context binaries from mutable references, inconsistent with SHA-pinning already established in gerrit-verify.yaml","Removed environment variables and TOML keys are silently ignored or generically warned, including security/store-critical surfaces like TICKETS_TRACKER_DIR and REBAR_MCP_ALLOW_RECONCILE_LIVE"]},"digest_hash_version":1,"model":"bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-opus-4-8","schema":"ticket_digest_v1"},"env_id":"b2b5c498-2f67-4ae3-bafc-eca40294bec2","event_type":"TICKET_DIGEST","timestamp":1785818587984400682,"uuid":"55ecf2c2-8884-4378-bd3f-be65a5e68c7b"}